  "date": "2026-08-20",
  "purpose": "Build a deterministic (non-adaptive, non-learned) KV tiering scheduler on top of the now-safe Phase 12B-12E relocate+retire primitives, and measure whether dynamic placement changes during live decode produce a real throughput advantage.",
  "literal_verdict": "WORKS_BUT_NO_PERF_ADVANTAGE",
  "verdict_summary": "The scheduler mechanism itself is fully validated: dynamic-schedule output is byte-identical to every static configuration tested at the same sequence positions; every requested transition in the first end-to-end schedule applied correctly via the established relocate_layer+invalidate_graph_cache primitives; two independent runs against identical state produce an identical decision trace (deterministic); 56 back-to-back relocations showed no VRAM growth; an intentionally-impossible budget correctly failed closed; the mechanism generalized across Q5_1, a second model, ctx=16384, and a memory-pressure regime. But the static hot-set sweep underlying this decision (0/8/15/22/30 of 30 layers on GPU) showed throughput varying only ~21.9-24.3 tok/s -- KV placement is not the bottleneck at this model/context scale, so the scheduler's correct, stable, deterministic transitions add measurable per-transition cost without a compensating throughput win. This directly echoes the project's own prior Phase 6.2 finding of no bytes/token win at tested scale.",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/dynamic-tiering-scheduler/summary.json:decision_gate (literal source field, one of five predeclared allowed enum values; not synthesized or abbreviated -- the full literal string is exactly `WORKS_BUT_NO_PERF_ADVANTAGE`, shorter than the DYNAMIC_KV_TIERING_WORKS_BUT_NO_PERF_ADVANTAGE form referenced in the migration brief)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "productization_note": "Verified: `git grep` for scheduler_core / MEMBRANE_TIERING_ against product main returns no hits. This is a valuable negative result, not a claim that dynamic tiering is universally useless -- the finding is scoped explicitly to the tested model/context regime (SmolLM2-135M/360M, GTX 1650, contexts up to 65536). The scheduler's own next_step_recommendation explicitly says NOT to invest in policy sophistication until a regime where KV placement actually is the bottleneck is found -- which became Phase 12G's task.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "NVIDIA GTX 1650 (4096 MiB VRAM), Vulkan backend",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-135M-Instruct",
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
  ],
